# Tests — NDA-MUT N-5 term and survival

Assertion-based tests for `NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd`. Every branch of the two
exception hierarchies (`survival_end_date` and `obligations_subsist`) is
covered, and both sides of every date threshold are tested: the last day of
the survival period and the day after, the last day of holding and the day
after, notice served one day before and one day after the point at which 30
days' notice still expires inside the term.

Three families of test exist specifically to catch encoding defects that the
type checker cannot see:

* **Composition of N-5.1 into N-5.2.** Early termination must pull the
  survival end date *earlier*. `EarlyTermination` asserts 2028-02-09, three
  years from the actual end, and not 2029-07-01, three years from the
  two-year anniversary.
* **The N-5.3 / N-5.4 contrast.** On otherwise identical facts, a trade
  secret yields **no** end date and personal data yields a computed one.
  `TradeSecretIndefinite` and `PersonalDataCeased` are that pair.
* **Trap 1, exceptions not inheriting their parent's condition.** Each
  exception's discriminating input is set while its class input is left
  false, so an exception missing its own condition would fire and the base
  answer would change. `CeasedDateIgnoredWhenNotPersonalData` and
  `NotTradeSecretJudgementIgnored` are those tests.
* **The in-term regime is not the post-expiry tail.** N-5.2 and its two
  exceptions measure only the period after expiry or termination, so every
  N-5.3 / N-5.4 exception repeats `assessment_date > agreement_end_date`.
  `N5_4_CeasedDuringTermStillBound` (CE-0017) and
  `N5_3_TradeSecretLapsedDuringTerm` (CE-0018) assess both exceptions at a
  date inside the term, where the obligations must subsist whatever those
  inputs say.
* **A notice cannot precede the Agreement.** `N5_1_NoticeBeforeEffectiveDate`
  (CE-0019) serves notice six months before the Effective Date; the right
  N-5.1 confers does not yet exist, so the full term runs.
  `N5_1_NoticeOnEffectiveDate` is the inclusive side of that floor.
* **Nor can the obligations.** `N5_1_AssessmentBeforeEffectiveDate` (CE-0030)
  assesses a date eighteen months before the Effective Date, and the day
  before it: N-5.1 makes the Agreement take effect on the Effective Date, so
  the N-3 obligations do not subsist before then, however far back N-2.1
  reaches for the information they attach to.

> Using NdaSurvival

## N5_1_FullTerm

N-5.1 base: the Agreement runs 2 years from the Effective Date where no party
serves notice, and N-5.2 then adds 3 years.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_FullTerm:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_FullTerm:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_2_LastDayOfSurvival

The survival end date is the last day on which the obligations bind.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_2_LastDayOfSurvival:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_2_LastDayOfSurvival:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2029-07-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_2_DayAfterSurvival

The other side of the same threshold.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_2_DayAfterSurvival:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_2_DayAfterSurvival:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2029-07-02|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = false
```

## N5_1_EarlyTermination

N-5.1 and N-5.2 compose. Notice on 2025-01-10 ends the Agreement 30 days
later, on 2025-02-09, and the 3 years of N-5.2 run from **that** date. The
survival therefore ends on 2028-02-09 — earlier than the 2029-07-01 the
two-year anniversary would have produced.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_EarlyTermination:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_EarlyTermination:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2025-01-10|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2025-02-09|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2028-02-09|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_1_EarlyTerminationSurvivalExpired

The same early termination, assessed after the shortened survival has run.
Had the survival been measured from the two-year anniversary the obligations
would still bind here.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_EarlyTerminationSurvivalExpired:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_EarlyTerminationSurvivalExpired:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2025-01-10|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2028-02-10|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2028-02-09|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = false
```

## N5_1_NoticeTooLateToShortenTerm

Notice served on 2026-06-20 expires on 2026-07-20, after the second
anniversary, so the Agreement is not "terminated earlier" and the ordinary
expiry stands.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_NoticeTooLateToShortenTerm:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_NoticeTooLateToShortenTerm:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2026-06-20|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-06-25|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
```

## N5_1_NoticeExpiringExactlyOnExpiry

Notice on 2026-06-01 expires on 2026-07-01, the day the Agreement expires
anyway. That is not earlier, so the ordinary expiry governs. This is one side
of the "terminated earlier" threshold.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_NoticeExpiringExactlyOnExpiry:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_NoticeExpiringExactlyOnExpiry:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2026-06-01|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-06-25|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
```

## N5_1_NoticeOneDayEarlier

The other side of that threshold: notice one day earlier expires on
2026-06-30, which is earlier, so it terminates the Agreement and pulls the
survival back to 2029-06-30.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_NoticeOneDayEarlier:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_NoticeOneDayEarlier:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2026-05-31|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-06-25|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-06-30|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-06-30|
```

## N5_1_MonthEndRounding

An Effective Date of 29 February is the month-end case where Catala date
addition is ambiguous and would raise without a declared rounding mode. The
scope declares `date round up`, so the two-year term ends on 2026-03-01 and
the survival on 2029-03-01.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_MonthEndRounding:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_MonthEndRounding:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-02-29|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-03-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-03-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_3_TradeSecretIndefinite

N-5.3: the 3-year arithmetic is disapplied and **no** end date is produced.
The obligations still bind seventy years on, because the information remains
a trade secret. A module that answered "three years" here would be asserting
the one thing the clause contradicts.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretIndefinite:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretIndefinite:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: true
      -- assessment_date: |2099-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Absent
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_3_TradeSecretNoLongerRemains

The second judgement input doing its work: the information was a trade secret
but no longer is, so the N-5.3 obligations have ended. Still no end date is
produced — the module cannot know the date on which it ceased.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretNoLongerRemains:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretNoLongerRemains:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2027-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Absent
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = false
```

## N5_3_TradeSecretWithEarlyTermination

N-5.3 disapplies N-5.2's arithmetic but not N-5.1's term, so the Agreement
still ends when notice says it does, and still no expiry date is produced.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretWithEarlyTermination:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretWithEarlyTermination:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2025-01-10|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: true
      -- assessment_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2025-02-09|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Absent
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_3_NotTradeSecretJudgementIgnored

Trap 1. The "remains a trade secret" judgement is true but the information is
not characterised as a trade secret, so N-5.3 must not fire and the N-5.2
base must govern. An exception written without its own condition would return
`Absent` here.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_3_NotTradeSecretJudgementIgnored:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_3_NotTradeSecretJudgementIgnored:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: true
      -- assessment_date: |2027-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_4_PersonalDataStillHeld

N-5.4: while the Recipient still holds the personal data no end date has
arisen, and the obligations bind however long that is.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataStillHeld:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataStillHeld:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2099-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Absent
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_4_PersonalDataCeased

The N-5.3 / N-5.4 contrast. On facts differing only in which class the
information falls into, N-5.4 produces a determinate end date — the date the
Recipient ceased to hold the data — where N-5.3 produced none. Here it
shortens the survival: 2027-03-15 is well before the N-5.2 date of
2029-07-01.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataCeased:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataCeased:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2027-03-15|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2027-03-15|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2027-03-15|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_4_PersonalDataCeasedDayAfter

The other side of the N-5.4 threshold.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataCeasedDayAfter:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataCeasedDayAfter:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2027-03-15|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2027-03-16|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2027-03-15|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = false
```

## N5_4_PersonalDataCeasedAfterThreeYears

N-5.4 can lengthen as well as shorten: holding personal data past the N-5.2
three years keeps the obligations running to the date holding ceases.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataCeasedAfterThreeYears:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_4_PersonalDataCeasedAfterThreeYears:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2031-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2030-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2031-01-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_4_CeasedDateIgnoredWhenNotPersonalData

Trap 1. A date of ceasing to hold is on file but the information is not
personal data, so N-5.4 must not fire and the N-5.2 base must govern. An
exception written without its own condition would return 2027-01-01 here.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_4_CeasedDateIgnoredWhenNotPersonalData:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_4_CeasedDateIgnoredWhenNotPersonalData:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2027-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2028-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_34_BothStillHeldNotTradeSecretAnyMore

Both exceptions bear on the same information. The trade secret has lapsed but
the Recipient still holds the personal data, so the obligations subsist on
the N-5.4 ground: neither clause disapplies the other.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_34_BothStillHeldNotTradeSecretAnyMore:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_34_BothStillHeldNotTradeSecretAnyMore:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2099-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Absent
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_34_BothTradeSecretAfterCeasingToHold

The mirror case: holding has ceased but the information remains a trade
secret, so the obligations subsist on the N-5.3 ground and no end date is
produced even though N-5.4 alone would have produced 2027-01-01.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_34_BothTradeSecretAfterCeasingToHold:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_34_BothTradeSecretAfterCeasingToHold:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2027-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: true
      -- assessment_date: |2030-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Absent
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_34_BothNeitherGroundRuns

Both exceptions apply and neither ground still runs, so the obligations have
ended. This is the third branch of the combined limb.

The end date is now produced rather than withheld. Once the trade-secret
limb has lapsed the only period still capable of running is N-5.4's, whose
terminus is the recorded date holding ceased — so 2027-01-01 is the answer,
and `Absent` would assert indefiniteness on the strength of a limb that has
stopped running.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_34_BothNeitherGroundRuns:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_34_BothNeitherGroundRuns:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2027-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2027-01-02|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2027-01-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = false
```

## N5_34_BothLastDayOfHolding

The N-5.4 boundary inside the combined limb, on its inclusive side, and the
same determinate end date as the day after.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_34_BothLastDayOfHolding:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_34_BothLastDayOfHolding:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2027-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2027-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2027-01-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_4_CeasedDuringTermStillBound

**CE-0017.** The Recipient deletes its copy of the personal data on
2025-01-01, six months into a term running to 2026-07-01, and the question is
asked on 2025-06-01, thirteen months before the Agreement expires. N-5.4 is
an exception to N-5.2, and N-5.2 measures only the period after expiry or
termination, so it cannot discharge an obligation N-3.1 and N-3.2 impose
while the Agreement is on foot: the obligations subsist. The end date is the
end of the Agreement — the N-5.4 tail was exhausted before it began, and
N-5.2 says the obligations "survive" expiry, so no reading puts the
confidentiality end date before 2026-07-01. The old encoding answered
`obligations_subsist = false` and `survival_end_date = 2025-01-01`.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_4_CeasedDuringTermStillBound:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_4_CeasedDuringTermStillBound:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2025-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2025-06-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_4_CeasedDuringTermAssessedAfterExpiry

The other side of that pair. The same facts assessed one day after expiry:
the N-5.4 tail is exhausted, so the obligations have ended — on the end of
the Agreement and not on 2025-01-01, which is the date the encoding must not
produce.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_4_CeasedDuringTermAssessedAfterExpiry:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_4_CeasedDuringTermAssessedAfterExpiry:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2025-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-07-02|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = false
```

## N5_3_TradeSecretLapsedDuringTerm

**CE-0018.** The information was a trade secret when disclosed and has ceased
to be one; it has not become public, so N-2.3(a) does not take it outside the
definition of Confidential Information, and it is not personal data. Asked on
2025-06-01, inside the term: N-5.3 is an exception to N-5.2 and so reaches
only the post-expiry tail, and N-3.1 and N-3.2 bind of their own force until
then. The obligations subsist. No end date is produced, because N-5.3 confers
none and the scope takes no input for the date the status lapsed. The old
encoding made the judgement input the whole of the answer and reported the
obligations extinguished with the Agreement still on foot.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretLapsedDuringTerm:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_3_TradeSecretLapsedDuringTerm:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2025-06-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Absent
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_34_BothGroundsLapsedDuringTerm

The combined limb under the same discipline: both classes apply, the trade
secret has lapsed and the data was deleted on 2025-01-01, and the question is
asked inside the term. Neither exception can reach back past expiry, so the
obligations subsist and the end date is the end of the Agreement.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_34_BothGroundsLapsedDuringTerm:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_34_BothGroundsLapsedDuringTerm:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2025-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: true
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2025-06-01|
    }
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_1_NoticeBeforeEffectiveDate

**CE-0019.** Notice purporting to terminate is served on 2024-01-01, six
months before the Effective Date of 2024-07-01. N-5.1 confers the right to
terminate on 30 days' notice on "either party" to an Agreement that "takes
effect on the Effective Date", so the right does not exist yet and the notice
bites on nothing; "terminated earlier" means earlier than the 2-year expiry,
not earlier than commencement. The full term therefore runs to 2026-07-01 and
N-5.2's three years to 2029-07-01. The old encoding compared notice + 30 days
against the anniversary with no floor at the Effective Date, and reported an
Agreement that ended on 2024-01-31 — five months before it began — carrying
that impossible date into N-5.2.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_NoticeBeforeEffectiveDate:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_NoticeBeforeEffectiveDate:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2024-01-01|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2025-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_1_NoticeOnEffectiveDate

The inclusive side of that floor. Notice served on the Effective Date itself
is served under an Agreement that has taken effect, so it is effective and
ends the Agreement 30 days later, on 2024-07-31, with the survival running to
2027-07-31.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_NoticeOnEffectiveDate:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_NoticeOnEffectiveDate:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Present content |2024-07-01|
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2025-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2024-07-31|
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2027-07-31|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N3_ObligationsSubsistOnLastDayOfTerm

The boundary between the two regimes, on the in-term side. The Agreement is
in force up to and including its end date, so `n3_in_term` governs there and
no N-5 exception can be reached; the day after, N-5.2 and its exceptions take
over. Both limbs are exercised on facts where the N-5.4 exception would
answer differently if it were allowed to reach inside the term.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN3_ObligationsSubsistOnLastDayOfTerm:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN3_ObligationsSubsistOnLastDayOfTerm:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2024-08-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2026-07-01|
    }
  assertion r.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
```

## N5_1_AssessmentBeforeEffectiveDate — CE-0030

N-5.1 makes the Agreement take effect on the Effective Date, and the N-3
obligations are obligations of the Recipient *under this Agreement*, so nothing
in N-3 binds before then. The question is a live one: N-2.1 makes information
disclosed "whether before or after the date of this Agreement" Confidential
Information, so a dispute about a disclosure eighteen months before the
Effective Date is squarely within the Agreement — but the obligations did not
subsist when it was made. The in-term limb had no lower bound and answered
`true` for every date in history.

The three dates pinned here are the day before the Effective Date, the
Effective Date itself, and a date a year and a half before it, so the floor is
tested on both sides as well as far outside.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_AssessmentBeforeEffectiveDate:
  output long_before content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd
  output day_before content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd
  output on_effective_date content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_AssessmentBeforeEffectiveDate:
  definition long_before equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2023-01-01|
    }
  definition day_before equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2024-06-30|
    }
  definition on_effective_date equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: false
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Absent
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2024-07-01|
    }
  assertion long_before.obligations_subsist = false
  assertion day_before.obligations_subsist = false
  assertion on_effective_date.obligations_subsist = true
  assertion long_before.agreement_end_date = |2026-07-01|
  assertion long_before.survival_end_date = Present content |2029-07-01|
```

The floor is the Effective Date and not the date of expiry, so it does not
disturb the post-expiry tail: personal data whose holding ceased before the
Agreement was made still leaves the obligations subsisting throughout the term.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestN5_1_FloorDoesNotDisturbTheTail:
  output r content NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd

scope TestN5_1_FloorDoesNotDisturbTheTail:
  definition r equals
    output of NdaSurvival.SurvivalEnd with {
      -- effective_date: |2024-07-01|
      -- termination_notice_date: Absent
      -- is_personal_data: true
      -- date_ceased_to_hold: Present content |2024-01-01|
      -- information_is_trade_secret: false
      -- information_remains_trade_secret: false
      -- assessment_date: |2025-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.obligations_subsist = true
  assertion r.survival_end_date = Present content |2026-07-01|
```
